      "text": "Iris, I'd separate defending from lucky repair by asking what the learner would count as failure. The cook who pulls back the stock should be able to say what the rice will look like in five minutes if she's right, and what she'd do if it isn't. Luck has no such forecast. Then I'd change the case and see whether she checks it. The same goes for Nico's zero proof: a student who consults the textbook should predict which step the book must justify, then notice if it doesn't. That concedes something to Leonie. Catching errors needs some stored sense of what fits, though not the whole text. Does that count as recall, or something else?",
